1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,600
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,030
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:06,170
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:07,760
I've been a line cook

5
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,080
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:11,210
Standing on a hard kitchen
floor,

7
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:12,590
ten hours a shift.

8
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:13,670
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,460
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,590
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:19,180
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,710
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:21,620
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:22,700
This is different.

15
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:23,330
Tight.

16
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:23,940
Full.

17
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:24,850
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:26,820
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:27,870
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:29,100
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:30,150
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,370
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:33,840
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:34,670
At three months,

25
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:35,750
give it six.

26
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,080
At six months,

27
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,660
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:39,750
At a year,

29
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,590
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:42,690
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:44,230
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:45,680
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:46,880
Every session,

34
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,400
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:49,950
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:51,330
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:53,050
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:54,380
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,400
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,570
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,570 --> 00:00:58,800
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,680
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:03,080
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,670
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:05,760
operation to go back

46
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,230
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:08,180
I said no.

48
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,710
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:10,690
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:12,330
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:14,580
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:16,390
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:18,260
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:19,780
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,340
couldn't stand at the
grill long enough

56
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:22,840
to finish a lunch rush,

57
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,940
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,400
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:29,050
It woke me at night,

60
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:31,090
and it turned ordinary
things,

61
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,340
like getting in the car

62
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,670
or up off the couch,

63
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:34,700
into a decision.

64
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:36,060
Some nights I had to sit

65
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:36,940
on a milk crate by

66
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:38,730
the dish pit between
tickets.

67
00:01:38,830 --> 00:01:40,100
After a long and serious

68
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:40,930
talk with my wife,

69
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:42,480
I went back in one more
time.

70
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:43,980
That was the fourth set

71
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,500
of X-rays on this knee.

72
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:47,390
And like the three before
it,

73
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:49,550
the answer was everything
looks great.

74
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:51,710
No loosening, no
infection,

75
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:52,630
nothing wrong.

76
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:53,980
Only this time there

77
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,190
was no new number.

78
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:56,420
Nobody said

79
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,800
give it another six
months.

80
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,690
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:00,960
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,040
lot for a while.

83
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,500
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:04,980
Then explain this.

85
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:07,380
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:08,830
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,190
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,330
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:15,070
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,180
with my leg up,

91
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,800
trying to find any angle
where

92
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,910
it didn't feel like
something

93
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:21,440
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

94
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,060
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

95
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:25,870
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

96
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:26,920
And I just thought,

97
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,550
is this really my life
now?

98
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,180
Thirty years on that line,

99
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:31,430
and this is how it ends?

100
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:32,880
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,750
So I made myself a
promise.

102
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:35,630
I wouldn't go a day

103
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:37,130
without looking for an
answer.

104
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:38,960
And when I found one,

105
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,060
I'd share it with everyone

106
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,280
going through the same
thing.

107
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:42,910
So I got my laptop

108
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,550
out and went looking.

109
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:45,990
Not for a product.

110
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:47,120
For an explanation.

111
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,220
Mayo Clinic forums,

112
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:51,640
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

113
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,100
doctor videos, medical
animations.

114
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,960
And that's when I found a
video

115
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,690
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

116
00:02:57,730 --> 00:02:59,390
Steven Salinger,

117
00:02:59,390 --> 00:03:00,500
whose own wife had been

118
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,740
through exactly this.

119
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:04,310
But before I say anything
else,

120
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:05,860
I want to be straight with
you.

121
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,080
You've already had
something work fast.

122
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:08,940
The ice.

123
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,640
The first week of a new
pill.

124
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:12,070
The good day after a
session.

125
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:13,540
Then it wore off.

126
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:15,970
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

127
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:17,430
Fast relief

128
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:18,360
isn't relief.

129
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,990
It's a preview.

130
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,550
So I'm not going to tell

131
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:22,860
you this works fast.

132
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:23,750
It doesn't.

133
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:25,940
But if you're willing to
be patient,

134
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,130
and to look at what's
going

135
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:28,370
on around your new knee

136
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:30,070
instead of inside it,
there

137
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:32,180
is a real reason it still
hurts.

138
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:34,430
And something you can do
about it.

139
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:36,740
Let me explain what he
said,

140
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,690
because this is what
changed

141
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:39,900
everything for me.

142
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:41,930
He started with the
basics.

143
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:43,680
A knee replacement takes
out

144
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,270
the worn joint surfaces

145
00:03:45,270 --> 00:03:47,130
and puts in metal and
plastic.

146
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:49,150
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

147
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,610
you had before the
operation.

148
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,280
That part I already knew.

149
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,690
But then he explained
something

150
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:55,090
nobody had ever told me.

151
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:56,170
He said,

152
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:57,670
think about a swollen foot

153
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:58,730
inside a shoe.

154
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:00,340
The shoe didn't shrink.

155
00:04:00,590 --> 00:04:02,790
Your foot is taking up
more room,

156
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,370
so everything feels
cramped

157
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:05,870
and tight and squeezed.

158
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,050
Your new knee sits

159
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:08,670
in a limited space with
living

160
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:10,360
tissue packed all around
it.

161
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,860
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

162
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,590
had to work through that
tissue.

163
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,870
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

164
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:19,680
At first that's normal.

165
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:20,870
But in some people

166
00:04:20,870 --> 00:04:22,380
that swelling can stay
switched

167
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,290
on far longer than
expected.

168
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:26,620
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,450
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:28,590 --> 00:04:30,140
So when you bend,

171
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,910
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,280
When you straighten,

173
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,770
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:35,910
That's the band.

175
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:38,480
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:39,680
And you start being

177
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,750
the one who says,

178
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:41,840
you go ahead.

179
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:42,880
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:43,050 --> 00:04:44,700
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,620
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:49,020
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,080
around the knee.

184
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:51,080
Worth doing,

185
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:51,930
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:51,970 --> 00:04:53,690
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:54,830
taking up room.

188
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:56,260
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:57,920
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:00,490
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:03,160
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,840
finally calms down,

193
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:06,440
it holds less fluid,

194
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,270
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,420
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,770
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,600
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,390
After two years of this,

199
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:17,970
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:20,200
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:22,240
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,100
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:26,610
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,360
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,930
compression braces,

206
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:32,420
creams, half of Amazon
really,

207
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,680
and all any of it gave

208
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,750
me was an hour.

209
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:36,110
I even looked at going

210
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:38,010
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

211
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,120
But at $200 a session

212
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,900
with nothing covered by
insurance,

213
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:43,240
that was a quick no.

214
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,330
Then one night I went

215
00:05:44,330 --> 00:05:45,600
back to that knee
replacement

216
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,070
group and actually read
it.

217
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:48,620
Thousands of people,

218
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:50,270
years out from surgery,

219
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:52,550
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

220
00:05:52,550 --> 00:05:53,890
nobody could explain.

221
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,980
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

222
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,660
the same thing kept coming
up.

223
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,750
This one device,

224
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,250
and people saying it was
the first

225
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:02,620
thing that made a
difference.

226
00:06:02,930 --> 00:06:05,100
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

227
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:06,430
alright, here it comes,

228
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,760
he's selling me something,

229
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,400
let me shut that down
right now.

230
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,070
I'm only here because I
made myself

231
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:13,080
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

232
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:13,980
that if I ever found

233
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:15,110
something that helped,

234
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:16,120
I'd say so.

235
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,470
It's called the KenRelief
Red

236
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:19,810
Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,900
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

238
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,260
It looked like the cheap

239
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,040
knee sleeves off Amazon

240
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,520
that did nothing for me.

241
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,720
But I went to their
website anyway,

242
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:29,620
just to see what all

243
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:30,650
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:31,010 --> 00:06:33,020
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

245
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:35,630
charge $200 a session for,

246
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:38,450
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

247
00:06:38,450 --> 00:06:39,520
in a wrap you plug

248
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:40,760
into the wall at home.

249
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:42,580
Two hundred and forty
lights.

250
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,290
Red at 660 nanometers

251
00:06:45,290 --> 00:06:47,930
and near-infrared at 850,

252
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:50,380
run together for the
strongest effect.

253
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:51,810
Four strength levels.

254
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,840
A five to thirty minute
timer.

255
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,410
Then I saw the guarantee.

256
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,670
Ninety days.

257
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,580
Results or your money
back,

258
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:01,130
no questions, no store
credit,

259
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:03,020
and you don't even send it
back.

260
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,500
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

261
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,150
days to change my mind.

262
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:08,650
There wasn't much to lose,

263
00:07:08,650 --> 00:07:09,670
so I ordered it.

264
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:10,990
Two of them, actually.

265
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:13,210
Only the right knee was
replaced,

266
00:07:13,210 --> 00:07:15,330
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

267
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:16,980
and I'd done it for two
years.

268
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,120
The left one was carrying
the difference.

269
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:19,760
When it came,

270
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:21,760
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

271
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:22,830
because I'd been let down

272
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:24,700
too many times to get
excited.

273
00:07:24,910 --> 00:07:26,650
What I felt was warmth.

274
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,830
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

275
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,760
More like it was coming
from inside

276
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,550
the knee and spreading
around it.

277
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:33,680
And that was it.

278
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,360
That was the whole
experience.

279
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,540
When I took it off,

280
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:37,640
I'll be honest,

281
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,350
nothing dramatic had
happened.

282
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,030
And after what that video
said,

283
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:42,780
that's exactly what I
expected.

284
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:44,460
What was different was

285
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:45,330
that for the first time

286
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:46,430
in two years

287
00:07:46,430 --> 00:07:48,120
I'd done something for my
knee

288
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,100
instead of to it.

289
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:50,420
Twenty minutes,

290
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:51,560
in my own chair.

291
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,200
No drive, no copay.

292
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:54,690
They say twenty minutes.

293
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,210
I did thirty,

294
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:57,510
twice a day,

295
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,450
lowest setting that first
week.

296
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,110
Once before my shift,

297
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:02,560
once after I got home.

298
00:08:02,770 --> 00:08:04,040
I put it on the calendar.

299
00:08:04,230 --> 00:08:05,210
The first week,

300
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:06,120
I couldn't have told

301
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,690
you if anything was
happening.

302
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,700
I tried not to get

303
